From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:07:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: wait 1 us after
 the touch chip select

Stock waits 1 us from asserting the FT3658's chip select to the first
clock: cs-clock-delay = <1> in the touch node's controller-data, in
Google's gs201-panther-touch.dtsi and in the Pixel 7's live device tree.
Upstream spells it spi-cs-setup-delay-ns, which the SPI core applies
after it drives a GPIO chip select, as this one is.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B (7.3.0-rc6), together with the previous
patch: the touch node has spi-cs-setup-delay-ns = 1000 in the live
device tree, and the controller probes (chip id 0x56, firmware 0x16)
and reports touches across the panel with no CRC errors.

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index b55b87138..8763b7b5b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -249,6 +249,8 @@ touchscreen@0 {
 		compatible = "focaltech,ft3658";
 		reg = <0>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <10000000>;
+		/* Stock's cs-clock-delay = <1>: 1 us from chip select to the clock */
+		spi-cs-setup-delay-ns = <1000>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&gpa7>;
 		interrupts = <0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
 		reset-gpios = <&gpp23 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
